<p:sld xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main"><p:cSld><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr><p:cNvPr id="1" name=""/><p:cNvGrpSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvGrpSpPr><p:grpSpPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="0" cy="0"/><a:chOff x="0" y="0"/><a:chExt cx="0" cy="0"/></a:xfrm></p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="2" name="TextBox 1"/><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="411480" y="228600"/><a:ext cx="10716203" cy="477054"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="none"><a:spAutoFit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:rPr sz="2400" b="1" i="0" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman"/></a:rPr><a:t>DIMENSIONAL SPACE IN DATA WAREHOUSING AND DATA MINING</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2400" b="1" i="0" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman"/></a:rPr><a:t> :</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr sz="2400" b="1" i="0" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="4" name="TextBox 3"/><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="411480" y="1015767"/><a:ext cx="10881360" cy="615553"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square"><a:spAutoFit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:rPr sz="1700" i="0" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman"/></a:rPr><a:t>Dimensional Space represents data using multiple dimensions or attributes so that complex business information can be analyzed from different perspectives</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1700" i="0" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman"/></a:rPr><a:t> :</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr sz="1700" i="0" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="5" name="TextBox 4"/><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="457200" y="1987153"/><a:ext cx="10789920" cy="4231928"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square"><a:spAutoFit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr marL="285750" indent="-285750" algn="just"><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="700"/></a:spcAft><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="q"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman"/></a:rPr><a:t>A dimension represents a perspective or characteristic used to analyze data, such as Time, Product, Customer, Location, or </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" b="0" i="0" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman"/></a:rPr><a:t>    </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman"/></a:rPr><a:t>Department.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="285750" indent="-285750" algn="just"><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="700"/></a:spcAft><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="q"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman"/></a:rPr><a:t>In a data warehouse, dimensional models organize data around measurable business facts and descriptive dimensions.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="285750" indent="-285750" algn="just"><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="700"/></a:spcAft><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="q"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman"/></a:rPr><a:t>A fact table stores numerical measures such as sales amount, quantity, profit, or cost, while dimension tables provide descriptive details.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="285750" indent="-285750" algn="just"><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="700"/></a:spcAft><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="q"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman"/></a:rPr><a:t>Dimensional space supports multidimensional analysis such as comparing sales by product, region, customer, and time.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="285750" indent="-285750" algn="just"><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="700"/></a:spcAft><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="q"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman"/></a:rPr><a:t>Data can be viewed at different levels of detail through operations such as drill-down, roll-up, slice, and dice.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="285750" indent="-285750" algn="just"><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="700"/></a:spcAft><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="q"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman"/></a:rPr><a:t>In data mining, dimensional information helps identify patterns, relationships, trends, groups, and useful knowledge from large datasets.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="285750" indent="-285750" algn="just"><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="700"/></a:spcAft><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="q"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman"/></a:rPr><a:t>It improves analytical queries, reporting, decision-making, and business intelligence by providing a structured view of data.</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>